  "findings": [
    "Fresh debugger stack stops at playerValues with a null authority: first-person NpcAnimation construction calls updateOblivionFirstPersonRoot -> oblivionProcessAction -> getPlayerValue before Actors::addActor.",
    "World::startNewGame now invokes its normal native actor admission after setupPlayer and before renderPlayer. Initial Player construction already provides action-1 and knocked0; no query fallback or new numeric rule is added.",
    "Full normal and ASan/UBSan engine checks each pass1857 tests; component code is unchanged after the linked decoder receipt.",
    "Instrumented newgame and distinct normal-process load each reach five real Player frames, save via F5, render the prison/HUD and exit0 with zero engine errors. Leak checks are disabled.",
    "Independent Python save decoding and actual load-complete live snapshot verify exact Player float storage bits/metadata and shared cursor at load; selected Player base fields, inventory, identity, passive ledger and process metadata survive resave. Source/restart PIDs differ and save/pristine/load hashes match.",
    "The full M10 audio course remains failed. The initial fixed wall wait was replaced by final-stage acknowledgement without removing expected command checks. SayTo, sound and weather commands execute, but Say with an unresolved speaker aborts on missing condition context; vanilla VM diagnostics are retained."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Readiness-only Lua module adds an observation hook; official record plugins remain unchanged. No complete native combat-input trajectory or FPS/controller/interruption coverage is claimed.",
    "These bounded positive courses do not waive failed fullaudio courses or other vanilla VM diagnostics. General Say/unloaded-speaker admission remains open.",
    "Automatic common-hit speech/resource/condition preparation/publication, quest predicate authority, INFO history/results and complete M15S4 acceptance remain open.",
    "No new original-game numerical oracle was required: this fixes ordering in the fork. Semantic inspection contracts are not described as pre-launch preregistration."
  ],
